<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Starodub</h1><p class="st-meta">1218 CE – 1460 CE (approx.) · capital Starodub</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small appanage on the Klyazma whose princely line produced the Pozharsky family, including the liberator of Moscow in 1612.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Starodub on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klyazma">Klyazma</a>, north-east of Vladimir, became the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-vsevolodovich-of-starodub">Ivan Vsevolodovich</a>, youngest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vsevolod-the-big-nest">Vsevolod the Big Nest</a>. He is usually said to have received it from his brother Yaroslav in 1238, after the Mongol invasion, rather than in 1218.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Starodub was a small forest principality within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vladimir-suzdal">Vladimir-Suzdal</a> lands and later a minor player between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>. Its prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fyodor-ivanovich-of-starodub">Fyodor Ivanovich</a> was killed at the Horde in 1330. The family divided its land into tiny estates held by branches such as the Pozharsky, Ryapolovsky, Gagarin and Romodanovsky princes.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>By the mid 15th century the Starodub princes had become servitors of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-moscow">Grand Duchy of Moscow</a>, and their land was merged into Muscovite territory. Their descendant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-pozharsky">Prince Dmitry Pozharsky</a> led the militia that freed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> from Polish occupation in 1612.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-starodub.jpg" alt="Principality of Starodub" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: uk:User:Siverec · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Starodub_Cathedral.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1218 CE – 1460 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Starodub</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ivan Vsevolodovich, Fyodor Ivanovich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old East Slavic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Starodub-on-the-Klyazma</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1339&amp;focus=principality-of-starodub" aria-label="Principality of Starodub on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5415 364 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Starodub lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5735 620L5878 523M5735 620L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5878 523h0M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5735 620h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5735 620h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1339&amp;focus=principality-of-starodub">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
